stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "Assembled, not issued" as DRAFT
    state "Issued with its manifest and hash" as ISSUED
    state "Receipt or signature recorded" as ACK
    state "Replaced by a later version" as SUPERSEDED
    state "Inside a statutory retention window" as HELD
    state "Under legal hold" as LEGAL_HOLD
    state "Clock expired, disposal allowed" as ERASABLE
    state "Content gone, tombstone kept" as TOMBSTONE

    [*] --> DRAFT: DS1 generator assembles from the master and the template in force
    DRAFT --> ISSUED: DS2 issued, manifest and hash written, bytes frozen
    DRAFT --> [*]: DS3 discarded before issue, nothing retained
    ISSUED --> ACK: DS4 acknowledgement or signature recorded
    ISSUED --> SUPERSEDED: DS5 a later version issued for the same subject and period
    ACK --> SUPERSEDED: DS5 the same after acknowledgement
    ISSUED --> HELD: DS6 a statutory retention clock applies
    ACK --> HELD: DS6 the same
    SUPERSEDED --> HELD: DS6 the same
    HELD --> LEGAL_HOLD: DS7 a legal hold is placed
    ISSUED --> LEGAL_HOLD: DS7 the same before any clock starts
    LEGAL_HOLD --> HELD: DS8 hold released, checked
    HELD --> ERASABLE: DS9 the longest applicable clock expires from the date of last entry
    ERASABLE --> TOMBSTONE: DS10 disposal under the tenant policy, audited
    TOMBSTONE --> [*]

    note right of ISSUED
        Bytes never change. A correction is a new
        version, and the superseded version is kept
        for its own retention class.
    end note

    note right of HELD
        An erasure request inside the window is
        deferred with the governing instrument
        named. Destruction is barred even after
        five years unless a register was carried
        forward into a new one.
    end note

    note right of TOMBSTONE
        Replay returns the tombstone: id, class,
        dates, basis and actor. Never a
        reconstruction of the content.
    end note
